# Global project rules

## General principles

- **Code comments and GitHub-facing text in English** — comments, commit/PR/issue text. Chat with the user follows project/user language rules (see `001-team-workflow.mdc`).
- **Strict typing** - use strict typing everywhere possible. Avoid `any`, use `unknown` when necessary.
- **Explicit access modifiers** - always specify access modifiers (`private`, `protected`, `public`). Do not use implicit modifiers.
- **Readonly for injected services** - all constructor dependencies must be marked `readonly`.
- **Comments in English** - all code comments should be in English and explain "why", not "what".

## Formatting

- **Indent / charset / line endings / trailing whitespace / final newline** — always follow the repository [`.editorconfig`](../../.editorconfig) for the file type being edited (do not hardcode indent sizes in rules).
- **Quotes**: single quotes for TypeScript/JavaScript (when not overridden by EditorConfig / project formatter)

## File structure

- One class/interface/type per file when practical
- TypeScript: file name matches exported symbol (kebab-case); use `index.ts` for re-exports
- C#: follow existing project naming (PascalCase types / files)
